@import copy from '../../components/copy.tscl'
@import docs from '../../layouts/docs.tscl'

<docs [title]="'Runtime'" [path]="'/reference/runtime'" [description]="'state, derived and shared: the functions you use in island scripts and stores.'">
  <h1>Runtime</h1>
  <h2>state(initial)</h2>
  <p>A reactive value. In an island's script, read and write it as a plain variable. In a <code>.ts</code> module, use <code>.get()</code> and <code>.set(value)</code>.</p>
  <div class="sample"><pre tabindex="0"><code verbatim>import { state } from 'clarusjs/runtime'

const count = state(0)   // { get(), set(v), initial }</code></pre><copy attach="interaction" /></div>
  <h2>derived(fn)</h2>
  <p>A value computed from other state; it updates when they change. Read-only.</p>
  <h2>shared(store)</h2>
  <p>In an island's script, a local name for a store (a module-level <code>state()</code>). Reads and writes go to the store, so every island using it stays in sync. On the server it renders a copy of the store's initial value.</p>
  <h2>render(name, props)</h2>
  <p>From <code>clarusjs/views</code>, in server code (a <code>load()</code>, a script importing the built server): renders any view under <code>src/</code> to an HTML string. The name is its path without the extension.</p>
  <div class="sample"><pre tabindex="0"><code verbatim>import { render } from 'clarusjs/views'

const html = await render('components/pill', { text: 'new' })</code></pre><copy attach="interaction" /></div>
  <p>Props are typed against the view's inputs by <code>.clarusjs/views.d.ts</code>, which <code>clarusjs check</code> writes: an unknown name or a wrong prop is a type error. Add that file to your <code>tsconfig.json</code>'s <code>include</code> to get the same types in your editor. The built server, <code>dist/server/index.mjs</code>, exports <code>render</code> too.</p>
</docs>
